// sic bitfield shorthand (sic.md §"Bitfields"): a bare flag resolves only where
// the bitfield type is determinable. `int a = Two;` has no bitfield context, so
// the flag is ambiguous — this must be rejected (`.xfail`). Write `Some::Two`.
bitfield Some { One, Two, Three };
int main() {
    int a = Two;       // ERROR: bare flag in a plain-int context
    return a;
}
